    {
      "parameters": {
        "model": "gpt-4o",
        "prompt": "You are a research assistant for an AI/ML monitoring pipeline called ResearchFlow. Your job is to help developers and researchers quickly assess new arXiv papers.\n\nGiven the full-paper summary below, respond with a JSON object and NOTHING ELSE — no markdown fences, no prose outside the object.\n\nRequired schema:\n{\n  \"what_it_does\": \"1-2 sentences on the core contribution\",\n  \"how_it_works\": \"1-2 sentences on the method or architecture\",\n  \"why_it_matters\": \"1 sentence on practical or research significance\",\n  \"relevance\": \"Low | Medium | High — for someone working on LLMs, RAG systems, or AI automation pipelines\",\n  \"tags\": [\"tag1\", \"tag2\"],\n  \"telegram_summary\": \"A single Markdown-formatted message combining all sections above, using the same emoji headings as before: 🔍 What it does, ⚙️ How it works, 📌 Why it matters, 🏷️ Relevance, 🗂️ Tags\"\n}\n\ntags must be an array of 1-3 strings chosen from: LLMs, RAG, Computer Vision, NLP, Reinforcement Learning, Robotics, AI Safety/Ethics, Multimodal, Agents, Infrastructure/MLOps — or a close match if none fit.\n\nTitle: {{ $json.title }}\nCategory: {{ $json.category }}\nFull paper summary: {{ $json.response.text }}\nPaper link: {{ $json.link }}\n\nReturn only the JSON object.",
        "options": {
          "responseFormat": "json_object"
        }
      },
      "id": "llm-summarize-id",
      "name": "OpenAI Summarize",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.openAi",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1750,
        420
      ],
      "credentials": {
        "openAiApi": {
          "id": "openai-cred-id"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "mode": "upsert",
        "collection": "arxiv_papers",
        "text": "={{ $json.parsed.telegram_summary }}",
        "metadata": {
          "metadataValues": [
            {
              "name": "title",
              "value": "={{ $json.title }}"
            },
            {
              "name": "url",
              "value": "={{ $json.id }}"
            },
            {
